---
import CalculatorLayout from '../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import NusGradeCalculatorWidget from '../components/calculators/NusGradeCalculator';

const relatedCalculators = [
  { title: "NUS CAP Calculator", path: "/nus-cap-calculator" },
  { title: "NUS GPA Calculator", path: "/nus-gpa-calculator" },
  { title: "NTU Grade Calculator", path: "/ntu-grade-calculator" },
];
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="NUS Grade Calculator (Target CAP)"
  description="Calculate the average grade you need for your remaining NUS modules to achieve your target Cumulative Average Point (CAP)."
  category="Academic & Education"
  categoryPath="/categories/academic"
>
  <NusGradeCalculatorWidget client:load slot="calculator" />

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>How to use the NUS Target Grade Calculator</h2>
    <p>
      If you have a specific Honours classification in mind (e.g., First Class, Second Upper), you need to know exactly what grades to aim for in your remaining semesters. The <strong>NUS Target Grade Calculator</strong> helps you determine the exact average grade point you need to achieve your goal.
    </p>
    <p>
      To use the calculator:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Current CAP:</strong> Enter your current Cumulative Average Point.</li>
      <li><strong>Current MCs:</strong> Enter the total number of <em>graded</em> Modular Credits you have taken so far. (Do not include S/U or CS/CU modules).</li>
      <li><strong>Target CAP:</strong> Enter your desired final CAP (e.g., 4.5 for Highest Distinction, 4.0 for Distinction).</li>
      <li><strong>Remaining MCs:</strong> Enter the total number of <em>graded</em> Modular Credits you plan to take before graduation.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The calculator will immediately tell you the average grade point required. If the required average is above 5.0, it will indicate that your target is mathematically impossible to reach.
    </p>

    <h3>Why is this useful?</h3>
    <p>
      Knowing your required average helps you strategize. For example, if your required average is 4.25, you know you need to score a mix of A- (4.5) and B+ (4.0) for your remaining modules. This can help you decide whether to exercise S/U options on borderline grades, or which modules to prioritize for studying.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          What does "Mathematically impossible" mean?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          Since the maximum grade point at NUS is 5.0 (A+ or A), it is impossible to average higher than 5.0. If the calculator says your target is impossible, it means that even if you score straight A+s for all remaining modules, you will not reach your target CAP.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          Should I include S/U modules in the "Remaining MCs"?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          No. You should only include modules that will be letter-graded and factored into your CAP. S/U modules do not affect your CAP calculation.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="related">
    {relatedCalculators.map(calc => (
      <li>
        <a href={calc.path} class="group flex items-center p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-white dark:hover:bg-slate-700 transition-colors">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2 text-slate-400 group-hover:text-teal-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 group-hover:text-teal-600 dark:group-hover:text-teal-400">{calc.title}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>
